    ('3.3 Network (WAN) and Leadership', 'Output', 'Established an inclusive and functional WAN that provides leadership development, mentorship, networking and support to young women and PWDs in aquaculture value chains', '•  Young women and persons with disabilities are willing and able to participate actively in WAN activities.\n\n•  WAN maintains inclusive, representative, transparent, and accountable governance.\n\n•  Qualified mentors and industry professionals remain available and committed to supporting members.\n\n•  Network activities, services, and communication platforms are accessible and responsive to members’ diverse needs.\n\n•  WAN secures adequate resources, partnerships, and institutional support for continued operation.', '•  Leadership disputes, elite capture, or inadequate representation of young women and persons with disabilities may undermine trust and ownership.\n\n•  Limited mentor availability, poor matching, or inconsistent engagement may reduce the value of mentorship and leadership development.\n\n•  Inaccessible activities, discrimination, harassment, or unsafe networking environments may exclude or harm some members.\n\n•  Insufficient resources, partnerships, and institutional ownership may make WAN dependent on project funding and unable to continue functioning over time.\n\n•  Some members may be unable to participate because of accessibility, mobility, caregiving, financial, or communication barriers.', 33, 'Number of Women in Aquaculture Network (WAN) groups established and active.', 'OP15', 'WAN', 'Location: Region, district, community Status: Strengthened (cooperative/cluster), Governance framework developed', 'Ecosystem strengthening', 'Program reports, Field and participant surveys', 'Applicable to CEL', 'Layered on #33: report as a status disaggregation of WAN groups/cooperatives. Planner PIII.6.'),
